@startuml
title Exact hot-cycle validation by progress-boundary removal
skinparam backgroundColor #FBFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #3D5366
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #EEF6FC
  BorderColor #4E7B99
}

rectangle "Published graph G = (N, E)" as original #DCEEFF
rectangle "Remove wait vertices" as waits #DDF2DF
rectangle "Remove bounded and\ndurable-yield transitions" as boundaries #FFF0C2
rectangle "Compute strongly connected\ncomponents of residual graph H" as scc #E8DDF5
rectangle "Any cyclic SCC?" as cyclic #FFD7CC
rectangle "Reject: a hot subcycle can\nbypass every progress boundary" as reject #F6BFC0
rectangle "Accept cycle-safety proof" as accept #C8E8D0

original --> waits
waits --> boundaries
boundaries --> scc
scc --> cyclic
cyclic --> reject : yes
cyclic --> accept : no

note bottom of accept #EAF7EE
H is acyclic iff every directed cycle in G
intersects a wait vertex or a bounded/yield edge.
This catches a smaller bypass cycle inside a safe-looking SCC.
end note
@enduml
